Z||000006||hugh||08-14-2000||09:48 PM||||GoKart,Thanks .The scoop is fully functional as an air inlet.The engine is a 350/345hp small block with a 425a transaxle.I don't know who built the car.<BR>HugGrrrfiero,I spent 5 years and over$20,000 building a 2 engine 1970 Chevelle.I did everything myself,except the bodywork and the upholstery.After that I feel like I'm cheating if I take any credit for something as nice as this car.Stupid,huh? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||08-15-2000||12:14 PM||||Wow! a 2 engine '70 Chevelle!  That's pretty cool and an engineering feat by all means!  Did you go with a side by side transverse, or an inline configuration, sorry just curious because I'm into Chevelle's too and slowly working on a '72 frame off project.<P>Well, I understand a little better where your coming from.  Unfortunately there's probably nothing anyone could say to make it easier.  I guess keep doing the little things to make it yours and better.  Be proud of it and that you do the work to keep it running great and top notch shape.  I think it's a really cool Fiero!||||reg||1
